{
  "info": {
    "name": "ID Document Extraction API v5.0",
    "description": "Multi-channel identity document extraction, ported from ID-Document-Extractor with Gemini replaced by local Ollama vision models. Channels, most-trustworthy first: barcode/QR (PDF417 AAMVA, Ethiopian FAN/QR) -> MRZ (ICAO 9303 TD1/TD2/TD3, checksum-verified) -> Ollama AI-vision crosscheck -> Ollama AI-vision universal fallback -> generic OCR label-alias sweep (the floor, never returns an empty profile). See idx/pipeline.py.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "id-extract-ai-agents-collection"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "job_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Populated automatically after a successful async extraction request"
    },
    {
      "key": "callback_url",
      "value": "https://webhook.site/REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-UNIQUE-ID",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Where the server POSTs the completed result. Get a free throwaway receiver URL at https://webhook.site to test, or point this at your own endpoint."
    },
    {
      "key": "doc_type",
      "value": "auto",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "passport | national_id | drivers_license | residence_permit | auto"
    },
    {
      "key": "universal_job_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Populated automatically after a universal async request"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Service Info",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            ""
          ]
        },
        "description": "Service info, pipeline architecture, supported document types/languages, and endpoint list."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Health Check",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Ollama model readiness, local OCR engine status, GPU info, active job count."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "List Pipeline Channels",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/agents",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "agents"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The 5 extraction channels in precedence order (barcode > MRZ > label-anchored OCR > VLM > signature sweep) with what each covers and how much it's trusted."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Extract ID (Async - poll)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/extract/id?doc_type={{doc_type}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "extract",
            "id"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "doc_type",
              "value": "{{doc_type}}",
              "description": "passport | national_id | drivers_license | residence_permit | auto"
            }
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "formdata",
          "formdata": [
            {
              "key": "file",
              "type": "file",
              "src": []
            },
            {
              "key": "file_back",
              "type": "file",
              "src": [],
              "disabled": true,
              "description": "Optional — back of card (AAMVA PDF417, Ethiopian ID QR). Order doesn't matter, both sides are classified by content."
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Default behavior: returns job_id immediately; poll GET /extract/status/{job_id} for the result.\n\nExtractions that fall through to the Ollama AI-vision tier can take several minutes on this hardware — for a production integration, prefer 'Extract ID (Async - callback_url)' instead of polling.\n\nSupported documents: National ID, Passport, Driver's License, Residence Permit.\nSupported formats: JPG, PNG, WEBP, BMP."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    const data = pm.response.json();",
              "    if (data.job_id) {",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('job_id', data.job_id);",
              "    }",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Extract ID (Async - callback_url)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/extract/id?doc_type={{doc_type}}&callback_url={{callback_url}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "extract",
            "id"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "doc_type",
              "value": "{{doc_type}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "callback_url",
              "value": "{{callback_url}}",
              "description": "http(s) URL the server POSTs the full completed result to when the job finishes. Retries 3x with backoff on delivery failure."
            }
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "formdata",
          "formdata": [
            {
              "key": "file",
              "type": "file",
              "src": []
            },
            {
              "key": "file_back",
              "type": "file",
              "src": [],
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Recommended for production integrations. Returns job_id immediately (no long-held connection, no polling) — the server POSTs the full result to callback_url once the pipeline finishes. Mutually exclusive with wait=true."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    const data = pm.response.json();",
              "    if (data.job_id) {",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('job_id', data.job_id);",
              "    }",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Get Job Status",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/extract/status/{{job_id}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "extract",
            "status",
            "{{job_id}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Poll for the result of an async extraction job. Uses the {{job_id}} collection variable set by an async extraction request. If the job was submitted with callback_url, the completed result also includes a callback_delivery field. The completed result's `document` field is the full ExtractedIDDocument (per-field value/raw/state/confidence/source/source_tier/agreeing_sources) — `extracted_data` is a flattened convenience view of the same data."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Extract ID (Sync)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/extract/id/sync?doc_type={{doc_type}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "extract",
            "id",
            "sync"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "doc_type",
              "value": "{{doc_type}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "formdata",
          "formdata": [
            {
              "key": "file",
              "type": "file",
              "src": []
            },
            {
              "key": "file_back",
              "type": "file",
              "src": [],
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Blocks and returns the full result directly in one call (equivalent to POST /extract/id?wait=true). If a barcode or MRZ resolves the document, this is typically fast (seconds); if it falls through to the Ollama AI-vision tier it can take several minutes — make sure Postman's request timeout is raised (Settings > General > Request Timeout) or this will time out client-side before the server finishes."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Delete Job",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/extract/job/{{job_id}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "extract",
            "job",
            "{{job_id}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Remove a job's record from the in-memory job store."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Universal Engine (any country / script / ID type)",
      "description": "5-agent Ollama team driven by universal_id_extraction_prompts.py, with every value checked by deterministic code: MRZ check digits, barcodes, national-ID checksums, calendar arithmetic and OCR grounding. mode=full (~1.5-2 min) or mode=fast (~15 s). Raise Postman's request timeout for the sync calls.",
